All submittals, upon filing, shall be classified as an "exempt," "minor," or "major" subdivision of land, as follows:
(1) Exempt subdivision. Any division of a lot or parcel into two (2) or more lots, building sites, parcels, or other divisions which has the following characteristics is exempt from the requirements of this chapter:
a. The sale of all portions of an existing lot or parcel to one (1) or more adjoining landowners for recombination into one (1) or more adjacent lots or parcels;
b. The sale of a part of an existing lot or parcel to an adjacent landowner is permitted for the purpose of combining it with the recipient's property, provided that the donor lot or parcel remains equal to or larger than the minimum lot size required by the zoning district;
c. The acquisition of rights-of-way by any governmental unit, municipality, the Georgia Regional Transportation Authority (GRTA), or the Georgia Department of Transportation (GDOT);
(2) Minor subdivision. Any division of a lot or parcel into two (2) up to five (5) lots, building sites, parcels, or other divisions, or the redivision of the same parcel that alters lot lines. This division must front upon an existing public or private road and shall be developed in accordance with existing conditions. Additionally, it shall not conflict with any provision of this chapter.
(3) Major subdivision. Any division of a lot or parcel into two (2) or more lots, building sites, parcels, or other divisions which is not classified as either exempt or minor.
(Ord. (W-4-24), § 2(Exh. A), of 10-8-24)

