9. City, county, or land lot lines accurately tied to the lines of the subdivision by distance and angles when such lines traverse the subdivision;
10. Road center lines, showing angles of deflection and standard curve data of intersection, radii, length of tangents and arcs, and degree of curvature;
11. Lot lines with dimensions to the nearest one-hundredth foot and bearings to the nearest minute, arcs, and chords and tangent or radii of rounded corners;
12. Front and rear structure or building setback lines; side setback lines may be noted upon the survey, but shall not be required to be shown upon each lot;
13. Lots or parcels numbered in numerical order or numbered in relationship to each phase of development; phase development lines;
